        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57b54994-05ea-5ff8-b5bf-c6c3c9489a25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Myrtus, Eustoma, myrtle, lisianthus, prairie gentian\n- Taxonomy: Myrtaceae, gentian family, flowering plants, genus\n- Concepts: fidelity, weddings, art, symbolism\n- People: Linnaeus\n\nFacts:\n- Linnaeus described the flowering plant genus Myrtus in 1753.\n- Myrtus, commonly called myrtle, is a genus of flowering plants in the family Myrtaceae.\n- Eustoma, commonly called lisianthus or prairie gentian, is a small genus in the gentian family.\n- From Roman times to the present, myrtle has been associated with fidelity and used in weddings.\n- Myrtle wreath crowns may be found in art as symbols connected with fidelity.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
